From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:22:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Present snapshots: a texture is the game's again once its
 copy has run

Backport of seedds/nxnative 0cad9500, the form in which PR #2153 landed
upstream. It replaces this patch's earlier version of the same fix.

With present snapshots on (Frame buffering, DM_PRESENT_SNAP), a present
that took a snapshot returned ticket 0, so the game's next acquire of that
texture waited for nothing and only the ring slot paced it. Xenoblade
Chronicles 3 then ran more frames ahead of the GPU than its swapchain holds
and rewrote per-frame uniform data that queued draws still read: its 3D
scene was one flat colour in 32 of 80 captures with 2 ring slots and 49 of
80 with 4 (LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1117).

A snapshot present now keeps its ticket, and the queue's receipt carries
the snapshot copy's event value (mtl_present's copy). The acquire of the
texture waits until that copy has run on the GPU
(mtl_present_wait_texture), not for the screen. Two differences from the
earlier version of this patch:

- The copy rides in the receipt instead of a 64-entry table keyed by
  ticket.
- nvnQueueFinish after a snapshot present waits for the copy too. The
  earlier version left it waiting by the ticket, which is the display
  link: a game that finishes its queue every frame was paced by the
  screen again (405 ms against about 1 ms with the display stalled for
  400 ms in t_present_snap ticket).

Adapted to the pin: nvn_queue.inc keeps the pin's single event per node
and its teardown-aware receipt wait; nvn_mtl.m keeps the pin's "present
snapshots off" log line; t_present_snap renames nvn_mtl.m's weak
nvn_hle_teardown in its translation unit, which hle_nvn.c defines, so the
test compiles at this pin.

(cherry picked from commit 0cad95002027592faa1859fc479081dc5c9a9288)

Upstream-Status: backport 0cad95002027592faa1859fc479081dc5c9a9288
Reason: Frame buffering (present snapshots) let Xenoblade Chronicles 3 rewrite per-frame data still in use: flat-colour frames
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1117

